\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Gate tests by reference point: discovery estimates (blue circles) and held-out declared tests (orange squares), 95\% intervals; the held-out verdict is at right (supported: \textsc  {held-out supported}; uninformative: not supported and below the test's MDE80; not supported: a declared test without a registered MDE80). Each row has its own scale: pp for the far jump, insider, branded title and least-distant fifth; pp per log unit for crowding; per 0.1 cosine and per 10 percentile points for the two same-author slopes. Compare replication status, not size. Crowding was registered; title style had been explored before registration; the other rows were found post hoc in discovery. Each held-out test was declared before any held-out estimate for that question was computed.}}{17}{figure.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
